! TRANSMIT: what this model honours, and what it refuses out loud.
!
! WHY THIS PROGRAM EXISTS.  bsv/README.md's "decoded but not executed
! (sets indicator 15, OP, and no-ops)" list has always named "Transmit
! backward/SWAP/multi-word".  Until 2026-09-22 only BACKWARD was true:
!
!   * the decoder matched sub-ops 010 (Transmit) and 110 (Swap) in one
!     condition and recorded NEITHER -- StretchTypes' Transmit struct
!     had no `swap` field -- so a forward SWAP arrived at the execute
!     stage indistinguishable from a Transmit and was executed as one;
!   * the execute arm moves exactly one word and never looked at the
!     count, so any multi-word Transmit moved one word.
!
! Both were SILENT: no indicator, no failure, a wrong store.  Neither
! was reachable from STRAP, because this assembler could not encode
! Transmit at all until TRANSMIT_CODES landed the same day -- which is
! why a claim in the README could stay false.  Demonstrated before it
! was fixed: "SWAPI,1,SRC,DST" left SRC alone and copied it into DST
! (0x9249249249249249) with OP clear.
!
! WHAT THE MANUAL SAYS THE COUNT IS.  Reference Manual printed p.30:
! the count is index J's bits 28-45, 0 meaning 2^18; or, with the
! immediate modifier (bit 56), instruction bits 51-54, where **0 MEANS
! SIXTEEN**.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SCOPE CHANGED ON 2026-10-18 AND SO DID THIS PROGRAM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Three of the six blocks below used to assert a REFUSAL and now
! assert that the operation HAPPENS.  MULTI-WORD AND DIRECT-COUNT
! TRANSMIT ARE BUILT: printed p.4 line 28 of MCP's bootstrap is an
! eleven-word direct-count transmit -- "MOVE MCP IPL" -- so the
! conservative refusal was stopping IBM's operating system from
! moving itself into storage.  decks/transmit_multiword.strap is the
! deck that pins the new behaviour in detail, against all five of
! p.30's rules; this one keeps its original job, which is the SCOPE:
! one block per rule, hanging at the first that is wrong.
!
! WHAT IS STILL REFUSED, and that is now ONE thing: SWAP, in either
! direction.  BACKWARD TRANSMISSION WAS BUILT ON 2026-10-22, for the
! same reason multi-word and direct-count were: printed p.19 line 41
! of MCP's initialization is "TB,3,0.0($11),0.0($13) -MOVE BIASED
! CTS", and with an IOCD deck on the tape the boot run reaches it.
! Reference Manual printed p.30 specifies the whole difference as one
! sign -- "obtained by DECREMENTING the previous addresses by one.
! The starting addresses specified in the instruction are therefore
! the addresses of the LAST word in each of the two storage areas" --
! so block 6 below now asserts that the operation HAPPENS.  Four of
! the six blocks have now flipped, and block 2 is the only refusal
! left.
!
! THE OLD TEXT IS KEPT BELOW because the history is the point of the
! file -- a claim in bsv/README.md that was two-thirds false, found by
! writing this program.  What changed is which third.
!
! A DIRECT COUNT USED TO BE REFUSED WHOLESALE, "deliberately
! conservative: the count register is never read here, so the arm
! cannot know whether a direct count is one.  It therefore refuses a
! direct count of one that it would have executed correctly."  The arm
! now reads the register, so block 5 loads it first.
!
! THE CASE THAT KEEPS THIS HONEST is still the first one.  If the fix
! were "OP on everything", block 1 would fail: TI with an immediate
! count of one must STILL STORE, and that is the shape jb_ax5b p.45
! actually uses (ax5b_16087_walk.strap).
!
! EACH BLOCK ISOLATES ONE RULE, and that is not decorative: the
! program hangs at the FIRST failing block, so an injection breaking
! several is only ever observed at the earliest.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD: hand-written from Reference Manual printed p.30 and
! the pocket card's TRANSMIT box.
!
! >>> THIS PARAGRAPH SAID "No listing this project has read prints a
! SWAP" AND IT IS FALSE TWICE OVER. <<<  Its backward half died on
! 2026-10-22 (MCP printed p.19 line 41 is a backward Transmit, and
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p19.strap reproduces it bit-exactly).  THE
! SWAP HALF DIED ON 2026-10-23, and by then two listings printed
! one: jb_ax4b routine 1246 TEST 2C, transcribed in
! decks/ax4b_1246_transmit_swap.strap, and MCP printed pp.40, 43, 45
! and 46, which carry NINE SWAPIs between them.
!
! AND "jb_ax4b section 146's own test plan ... remains untranscribed"
! was stale too: TEST 2A, 2B and 2C are all transcribed, and 2C's
! EXECUTION is now tested by decks/swap_scope.strap, which is where
! SWAP's semantics live.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
!
! ---- 1. TI, immediate count 1: HONOURED, the word moves -----------
START   TI,    1, SRC, DST1
        BOP,   $                     ! hang if OP came on: this one is legal
!
! ---- 2. SWAPI: HONOURED SINCE 2026-10-23, and this block used to
! ---- assert the opposite ------------------------------------------
! It read "SWAPI: refused.  The case that was silently wrong", and it
! was right for as long as nothing in the corpus executed a swap.
! MCP printed pp.40, 43, 45 and 46 carry NINE SWAPIs, and printed
! p.40's Y REELC executes two of them on the path a REEL card takes,
! so the refusal went from documented absence to blocker.  Forward
! SWAP is built; decks/swap_scope.strap is where its semantics are
! checked, including the overlapping-areas case that separates an
! exchange from a copy.  THIS BLOCK NOW ASSERTS THE OPPOSITE OF WHAT
! IT ASSERTED, which is why the old text is quoted rather than
! deleted.
! AND IT SWAPS ITS OWN PAIR, not SRC: an exchange EMPTIES the sending
! word, and blocks 3-6 all read SRC afterwards.  SRC2 holds the same
! pattern so the block still tests the same thing.
        SWAPI, 1, SRC2, DST2
        BOP,   $                     ! hang if OP came on: this one is legal
!
! ---- 3. TI, immediate count 2: HONOURED, TWO words move -----------
! This block used to assert a refusal.  Both words are checked, so a
! model that moved one word and called it done fails here.
        TI,    2, SRC, DST3
        BOP,   $
!
! ---- 4. TI, immediate count 0 = SIXTEEN: HONOURED -----------------
! p.30: "A zero count field indicates the maximum count of 16 full
! words."  The first and SIXTEENTH destination words are both checked,
! so a model reading zero as zero (moves nothing) and one reading it
! as one both fail.
        TI,    0, SRC, DST4
        BOP,   $
!
! ---- 5. T, DIRECT count: HONOURED, the count register is read -----
! The arm now reads index 1's count field.  Loading it first is the
! whole difference from the old block, which could not have been
! written at all while the register went unread.
        LCI,   $X1, 1
        T,     1, SRC, DST5
        BOP,   $
!
! ---- 6. TBI, backward: HONOURED, the word moves -------------------
! THIS BLOCK FLIPPED ON 2026-10-22.  It used to assert a refusal, and
! the note below is why it was written as TBI rather than TB -- kept
! because the reasoning is still what makes the block sharp:
!
!   "IT MUST BE TBI, NOT TB, and that was found by an injection
!   rather than by thinking.  TB is backward with a DIRECT count;
!   while direct counts were refused wholesale, removing the backward
!   check changed nothing and the block still passed.  TBI is
!   backward with an immediate count, so only the backward check can
!   refuse it."
!
! A COUNT OF ONE IS THE ONE CASE WHERE DIRECTION DOES NOT SHOW, and
! that is deliberate here: this file's job is the SCOPE -- does the
! arm accept the modifier at all -- and one word proves acceptance
! without depending on the stepping.  THE STEPPING IS PINNED
! ELSEWHERE: decks/transmit_multiword.strap steps 6 and 7 move five
! and three words backward and check every one, including the
! upper-end overlap printed p.30 says backward is *required* for.
!
! THE INJECTION FOR THIS BLOCK WAS REPLACED, NOT RE-RUN.  The old one
! removed the backward check, which means nothing now that the check
! is gone; the new one restores it ("t.backward == 1 || t.swap == 1"
! in StretchExecute's Transmit arm) and is caught here, at this
! block's BOP -- 004111.40, half-word 4243 -- with DST6 still zero
! and the step cap reporting "reached without halting".
        TBI,   1, SRC, DST6
        BOP,   $                     ! hang if OP came on: backward is legal
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- data ---------------------------------------------------------
! SIXTEEN source words, because block 4 moves sixteen.  Every
! destination area is far enough from the others that no block's
! transmit can reach into another's -- block 4's sixteen words are
! the reason that matters.
        SLC, (8)4200.0
SRC     DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        SLC, (8)4300.0
DST1    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! must RECEIVE src
        SLC, (8)4310.0
SRC2    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111   ! block 2's own sender
        SLC, (8)4311.0
DST2    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! must RECEIVE src2; SRC2 ends zero
        SLC, (8)4320.0
DST3    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! two words, both must receive
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)4400.0
DST4    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! sixteen words; first and last checked
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
DST4END DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)4500.0
DST5    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! direct count of one
        SLC, (8)4510.0
DST6    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! must RECEIVE src: TBI is honoured
        END, START
